  - Mathlib
  - formal-conjectures
  - Palomar
  - Erdős problems
  - MathOverflow
  - probability inequalities
abstract: >-
  Palomar-ready Lean 4 projects (Lean v4.36.0, Mathlib fc4f59e) for seven statements of
  google-deepmind/formal-conjectures whose proofs were first merged on Left to Solve: the Erdős–Taylor
  theorem on the planar random walk, Hadamard matrices of all orders 4k ≤ 664, the Erdős–Rado
  relation 𝔠 → (ω + n, 4)³, two results on Lebesgue constants (Erdős Problem 1129) and Erdős's bound
  Υ < √n (Problem 1130), and Erdős Problem 1044 in degrees 1 and 2. The proofs were written by Claude Code agents directed by the author, who
  reviewed the work and is responsible for it. The merged originals are archived in the companion
  repository left-to-solve-proofs. Version 1.1.0 adds six entries ported from the author's own
  repositories: five results first published there (a negative answer to MathOverflow 505921 (tanh Y tanh Z and tanh X are never
  stochastically ordered), Friedan's generalized entropy inequality and its quantum form (MathOverflow
  138395), a counterexample to Gillibert's Equal Halves conjecture, and Kimberling's Archimedean-copula
  inequality (MathOverflow 195959)), and a formalization of Ling's proof of Feige's inequality for every
  δ > 0 and of the lower bound of Samuels' conjecture.
